strator","notes":null}]},{"name":"Application Verification Stage","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"PAGE 3: QUESTION 17 - Online Gaming Application Form","tag":"Question","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-10-15","description":"One check box of Question 17 is not filled out. Kindly select the one and specify jurisdiction of Question 17.1 and resubmit the form.","notes":null}]},{"name":"Application Due Diligence Review","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"QPA/2024/00370 - Dmytro Basii - Passport","tag":"Passport","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-10","description":"Please provide a full scan of the bio and first page .","notes":null},{"title":"QPA/2024/00370 - Dmytro Basii - SOW","tag":"Source of Wealth","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-21","description":"SOW is not valid. Please submit a SOW along with certified supporting evidence in order to support the business.","notes":null},{"title":"QPA/2024/00370 - Dmytro Basii - Criminal Record","tag":"Criminal Record","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-10","description":"Please submit a criminal record that is not more than six months old.","notes":null},{"title":"QPA/2024/00370 - Dmytro Basii - SOW","tag":"Source of Wealth","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-10","description":"SOW is not valid. Please submit a SOW along with certified supporting evidence in order to support the business.","notes":null},{"title":"QPA/2024/02350 - George Van Zinnicq Bergmann - PHDF","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-10","description":"The PHDF must be signed and verified digitally. Please resubmit.","notes":null},{"title":"Compliance Officer","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-12","description":"No CO identified. CO, fluent in AML, to submit PHDF and relevant documentation, including a CV and letter of engagement","notes":null},{"title":"Business and Corporate Information Form","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Medium","due":"2025-03-12","description":"Applicant company was found to exist under a Master license. Amend question 7 accordingly and resubmit form","notes":null},{"title":"local director","tag":"Director's List","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-12","description":"At least one Local director required to be an executive director. Update role in portal","notes":null},{"title":"Company Details","tag":"Operations","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-13","description":"The registered domains must be operated by the Curacao registered applicant company and this must be stated correctly in the footer of each domain. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Player Registration","tag":"Player Registration","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-13","description":"The registration form does not require the player's name, address, country or DOB. This information must be collected at the latest prior to the first deposit. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Prohibited Jurisdictions","tag":"Prohibiited Countries","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-03-13","description":"Although the registered domains implement geo-blocking for restricted jurisdictions, players on hotspincasino are still allowed to choose Netherlands as their country of residence. Players residing in Curacao, the Netherlands (and any other countries part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands), USA, UN sanctioned countries and FATF blacklisted countries must not be allowed to register an account. Kindly amend.","notes":null}]},{"name":"Responsible Gaming","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"ID verification procedure","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"ID verification procedure","notes":null},{"title":"Account closure procedure","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Account closure procedure upon the operator becoming aware that the player is a minor post-registration.","notes":null},{"title":"Record-keeping","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Record-keeping","notes":null},{"title":"Language","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Must be available in English and target market language","notes":null},{"title":"Vulnerable gamblers","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"RG policy should include a structured process on flagging potential vulnerable gamblers","notes":null},{"title":"Indicators of problem gambling","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Must have a structured process for responding to indicators of problem gambling","notes":null},{"title":"Player profiling and Risk Assessment","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Establish player profiles to assess risk levels","notes":null},{"title":"Monitoring and intervention","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Adopt RBA to determine level of monitoring and intervention","notes":null},{"title":"Recording RG interactions","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-08","description":"Record all RG interactions in PAM system","notes":null},{"title":"Identification of vulnerable persons","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Procedure to follow for players identified as vulnerable persons","notes":null},{"title":"Cooling-off period","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Operator must offer players option to activate a cooling-off period","notes":null},{"title":"Cooling-off options","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Options for cooling-off must include duration and marketing opt-out at minimum","notes":null},{"title":"Self-Exclusion","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Operator must offer players the option to self-exclude themselves for a duration of at least 1 year","notes":null},{"title":"Deposit Limits","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Players must be able to set limits on the total amount they deposit","notes":null},{"title":"Training and Staff Readiness","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Operators must train customer service and Responsible Gaming staff to handle player interaction profesionally and effectively","notes":null},{"title":"Consumer Advertising and Marketing","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"Operators must not engage in irresponsible advertising","notes":null},{"title":"Internet Filtering Tools","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Low","due":"2026-04-30","description":"The operator is advised to remind adults that they should take precautions when sharing devices with minors","notes":null},{"title":"Notifications for concerning behaviours","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"High","due":"2026-05-08","description":"Operators may employ automatic or manual pop-up notifications in response to concerning behaviours","notes":null},{"title":"Initiating direct contact","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-04-30","description":"When a player exhibits behaviour that reasonably suggests they may be a Vulnerable Player, the operator must initiate direct contact","notes":null},{"title":"Other Limits","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"High","due":"2026-05-08","description":"Other limits may be considered including loss limits, time limits or wager limits, in line wth the operator's target player and/or market","notes":null}]},{"name":"Player Complaints","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"Recommencing ADR process with a different entity","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-08","description":"The policy must state that once the ADR process is completed it cannot be recommenced by either the player or the operator with another different ADR entity.","notes":null},{"title":"Recommencing dropped ADR processes","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-08","description":"The policy must state that in the event that the player drops out of the ADR process (but it has already begun) the player should not have the right to resurface the dispute in the future.","notes":null},{"title":"Restrictions on ADR escalation","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-08","description":"Provision of ADR services by the operator is mandatory. If the operator sets ADR parameters in order to prevent abuse (such as whether ADR must be undertaken before a player can initiate legal proceedings, the binding nature of the ADR outcome on the player, or whether there is a minimum claim value required for escalation to ADR), the CGA advises the operator to carefully consider these conditions and seek independent legal advice regarding any applicable civil legislation.","notes":null},{"title":"CGA's right to access records","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-08","description":"The policy must state that in light of the fact that the CGA reserves the right to request, at any time, access to records of complaints received as well as any disputes that are pending resolution, the operator shall ensure that such records are readily available at all times.","notes":null},{"title":"Right to make a complaint","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-08","description":"The policy must state that the player has the right to make a complaint regarding any part of their relationship with the operator, or any incident related to their participation in a game of chance. This includes (but is not limited to): 1. Deposit issues 2. Withdrawal issues 3. Bonus terms and conditions 4. Account closures or restrictions 5. Alleged errors or unfairness in game outcomes 6. Responsible gaming issues 7. Treatment of player balances 8. KYC and Verification 9. Data Protection 10. Technical or Software issues 11. AML concerns 12. Issues with minors 13. Fraudulent games 14. Fraudulent practices 15. License or regulation 16. Unfair terms and conditions","notes":null}]}]}]}